What it is: Built a fundamental CLI geography quiz game in C++ to practice string variables, console input/output, and conditional control flow.

How it works: Hardcoded questions and answers into variables, using sequential cin prompts and if-else branching to validate user input line by line.

Key learnings & takeaways:

Successfully handled basic terminal interaction and boolean evaluation.

Identified a couple of practical bugs early on—specifically case sensitivity (e.g., matching "london" vs "London") and std::cin stopping at whitespace.

Planned refactoring: The current version relies on repeated hardcoded blocks, so the immediate next step is to store questions in dynamic data structures (like std::vector or structs) and run them through a single for loop to make it scalabl
